<?xml version="1.0" encoding="windows-1251"?>
<!-- Widgets for the two-arm route prototype (iqm_arms.script).

     Samples iqm_arm, the SAME artwork the shipped arms style used before R2.20 -- not
     new art, and deliberately so. It already carries the two features this renderer
     depends on, both added while the arms style was live:

       * a SOFT TIP (ARM_TIP = 0.14 of the arm's length, tools/stroke-tex/build.py),
         so an arm fades out rather than stopping at a hard cut. Two rectangles cannot
         meet cleanly at a point; a soft end asks no question about where exactly it
         stops, which is what keeps the apex wedge from reading as a notch.
       * a tapered tail, so the outer ends do not stop dead in mid-air.

     stretch="1" is load-bearing: the rect is computed per frame from the projection
     and the picture has to follow it. Sizes here are placeholders. -->
<w>
	<arm_bar width="64" height="12" stretch="1">
		<texture r="224" g="196" b="122" a="255">iqm_arm</texture>
	</arm_bar>
</w>
